I have a complete picture. Here is the thorough report.

## Summary

This is a Spring PetClinic REST app. All owner-creation logic lives in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`. Address is a required `@NotEmpty` field, household duplicate/shared-household logic lives in three collaborators (`Households`, `HouseholdDuplicateValidator`, `HouseholdAssigner`), and address comparison is done via a normalize-and-key scheme inside `Households`. Note a significant gap flagged at the end: acceptance tests expect address *normalization* (abbreviation expansion + upper-casing) that does not exist in the production code.

---

## 1. Owner entity / model — the address field

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

`Owner extends Person`, `@Entity @Table(name = "owners")`. The address field:

```java
@Column(name = "address")
@NotEmpty
private String address;
```

Other relevant fields: `city` (`@NotEmpty`), `telephone` (`@NotEmpty` + E.164 `@Pattern`), `email` (`@Email`), `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and the household field:

```java
@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;
```

Getters/setters `getAddress`/`setAddress` (lines 68-74) and `getHouseholdId`/`setHouseholdId` (lines 116-122). `@PrePersist defaultRegistrationDate()` defaults registration date. `toString()` includes address (line 203).

---

## 2. Controllers handling owner creation (POST)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java` — implements `OwnersApi`, mapped at `/api`. This is the only POST-create endpoint (`addOwner`, backing `POST /api/owners`).

The `@Valid` validator is wired here:
```java
@InitBinder("ownerFieldsDto")
void initOwnerFieldsBinder(WebDataBinder binder) {
    binder.addValidators(ownerFieldsValidator);
}
```

The creation method:
```java
@PreAuthorize("hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)")
@Override
public ResponseEntity<OwnerDto> addOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerFieldsDto) {
    HttpHeaders headers = new HttpHeaders();
    Owner owner = ownerMapper.toOwner(ownerFieldsDto);
    String telephone = telephoneNormalizer.normalize(owner.getTelephone());
    if (!this.clinicService.findOwnerByTelephone(telephone).isEmpty()) {
        throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(telephone);
    }
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(ownerFieldsDto.getSharesHousehold())) {
        householdAssigner.assignSharedHousehold(owner);
    } else {
        householdDuplicateValidator.validate(owner);
    }
    owner.setTelephone(telephone);
    owner.setEmail(emailNormalizer.normalize(owner.getEmail()));
    this.clinicService.saveOwner(owner);
    OwnerDto ownerDto = ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner);
    headers.setLocation(UriComponentsBuilder.newInstance()
        .path("/api/owners/{id}").buildAndExpand(owner.getId()).toUri());
    return new ResponseEntity<>(ownerDto, headers, HttpStatus.CREATED);
}
```
Key ordering: telephone normalized + duplicate-checked, then household branch (shares → assign shared id; else → reject duplicate), then email normalized, then saved. Note: address is NOT normalized here — it is stored as mapped from the DTO.

`updateOwner` (lines 161-174) sets `address`/`city` directly from the DTO with no household re-check.

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java` — V2 only exposes `listOwnersPage` (GET/paging). No create endpoint.

---

## 3. Service layer for owners

Interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicService.java` (lines 56-63) — declares `findOwnerById`, `findAllOwners`, `findOwners(String, Pageable)`, `saveOwner`, `deleteOwner`, `findOwnerByLastName`, `findOwnerByTelephone`, and `findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase` (the last is the one household logic depends on).

Impl: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/service/ClinicServiceImpl.java`

```java
public void saveOwner(Owner owner) throws DataAccessException {
    if (owner.isNew() && owner.getCustomerCode() == null) {
        long sequence = ownerRepository.findAll().size() + 1L;
        owner.setCustomerCode(customerCodeGenerator.generate(owner.getLastName(), sequence));
    }
    ownerRepository.save(owner);
}

@Transactional(readOnly = true)
public Collection<Owner> findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase(String lastName) throws DataAccessException {
    return ownerRepository.findByLastNameIgnoreCase(lastName);
}
```
`findOwnerByTelephone` delegates to `ownerRepository.findByTelephone`. Repository interface: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java` declares `findByLastNameIgnoreCase`, `findByTelephone`, `findByLastName`, `save`, etc. Implementations exist under `repository/jpa`, `repository/jdbc`, `repository/springdatajpa`.

---

## 4. Validation — required-field / blank checks for address

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/OwnerFieldsValidator.java`

A Spring `Validator` (registered via the `@InitBinder` above) that rejects blank required fields including address:
```java
@Override
public void validate(Object target, Errors errors) {
    OwnerFieldsDto owner = (OwnerFieldsDto) target;
    rejectIfBlank(errors, "firstName", owner.getFirstName());
    rejectIfBlank(errors, "lastName", owner.getLastName());
    rejectIfBlank(errors, "address", owner.getAddress());
    rejectIfBlank(errors, "city", owner.getCity());
    rejectIfBlank(errors, "telephone", owner.getTelephone());
}

private void rejectIfBlank(Errors errors, String field, String value) {
    if (!StringUtils.hasText(value)) {
        errors.rejectValue(field, "required", "must not be blank");
    }
}
```
`StringUtils.hasText` treats null/empty/whitespace-only as blank → error code `"required"`, message `"must not be blank"`.

Second layer: Bean Validation `@NotEmpty` on `Owner.address` (model) and the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerFieldsDto` constraints derived from the spec (`address` `minLength: 1`, `required`). Validation failures surface as 400 via `ExceptionControllerAdvice.handleMethodArgumentNotValidException` (lines 187-223).

OpenAPI source of the address/required constraints: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml` `OwnerFields` schema (lines 2012-2018 for address; `required` list lines 2067-2072 includes `address`).

---

## 5. Household logic (duplicate detection + shared household id)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/Households.java` — the core identity/comparison helper.

```java
public List<Owner> findMembers(Owner candidate) {
    String key = key(candidate);
    return clinicService.findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase(candidate.getLastName()).stream()
        .filter(existing -> key.equals(key(existing)))
        .toList();
}

public String stableId(Owner owner) {
    return UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes(key(owner).getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8)).toString();
}

private String key(Owner owner) {
    return normalize(owner.getLastName()) + "\n" + normalize(owner.getAddress());
}

private String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```
Household identity = normalized(lastName) + "\n" + normalized(address). `stableId` = deterministic name-based UUID (v3) over the key. Candidate never includes itself (queries existing owners by last name).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/HouseholdDuplicateValidator.java` — duplicate detection:
```java
public void validate(Owner candidate) {
    if (!households.findMembers(candidate).isEmpty()) {
        throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(candidate.getLastName(), candidate.getAddress());
    }
}
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/HouseholdAssigner.java` — shared household id computation/back-fill:
```java
public void assignSharedHousehold(Owner candidate) {
    List<Owner> members = households.findMembers(candidate);
    if (members.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }
    String householdId = households.stableId(candidate);
